# PSR-6c2 — Harbor thin host + card mapper

## Intent

Prepare Harbor for durable G1 without cloning Denali/Urban catalog services:

1. **Card mapper** — `PublicCatalogTourInput` → `HarborSmokeCatalogCard` (city Event
   egress + JSON-LD), product-owned projection only.
2. **Thin HTTP host slot** — `configureHarborHttpHost` / `tryGet` / reset — ports
   typed for a future tour store; **API does not configure yet** (PSR-6c3).
3. **Smoke HTTP unchanged** — still seed-gated memory store (no false durable path
   without request-scoped tenant).

## Why host without wiring handlers

Smoke `catalogPort` has no `req`/`tenantId`. Real RLS needs host-bound routes
(or a later request-scoped factory). Shipping the slot + mapper first lets 6c3
bind `resolveProductTourStore` without inventing Harbor card shape under pressure.

## SDK adjunct

`createWorkspaceHttpHostSlot` gains `tryGet(): TPorts | null` so Harbor can detect
an unconfigured host without throwing `HARBOR_HTTP_HOST_NOT_CONFIGURED`.

## File budget

Harbor `src/http` stays ≤6 modules (clone detector). Mapper lives under
`src/catalog/`.

## Non-goals

- `configure-product-http-hosts` Harbor binding
- `isDurableEnabled` on Harbor HTTP
- Prisma / registration adapters
- Recert / tier promote

## Verify

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-6c2-harbor-thin-host-card-mapper-smoke.mjs
pnpm --filter @app-tour/workspace-harbor run test
pnpm --filter @app-tour/workspace-sdk exec node --import tsx --test test/http-plib-dg1.spec.ts
```

## Next

`PSR-6c3-api-configure-harbor-host` — generated façade + API configure + request-
scoped durable handlers (or port bridge).
